      "question": "The equation 3/x + 5 = -2x + c, where c is a constant, has no real roots. Find the range of possible values of c.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "5 - 2 sqrt(6) < c < 5 + 2 sqrt(6)",
      "steps": [
        "Multiply by x (x = 0 is not a root since 3/x is undefined there): 3 + 5x = -2x^2 + cx.",
        "Rearrange: 2x^2 + (5 - c)x + 3 = 0.",
        "No real roots needs discriminant < 0: (5 - c)^2 - 4(2)(3) < 0.",
        "(c - 5)^2 < 24, so 5 - sqrt(24) < c < 5 + sqrt(24), i.e. 5 - 2 sqrt(6) < c < 5 + 2 sqrt(6)."
      ],
      "images": [
